(7226282, 1116603, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Now that is either fantastic muscle control or something is/akin to Bells Palsy. If the later, awesome that you are brave, remain in good spirits and seeing the positive- it goes a long way. If it is supreme muscle control - Wow! The lighting and details are great in this portrait. There are great catch lights in the eyes that shows a cheerful sparkle. You have two asymmetrical subjects in the photo: the first is the ''emotions'' on the face and the second is the thumbs up &amp; thumbs down. This has very clearly met the challenge and is well done - should be in the top ten.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Now that is either fantastic muscle control or something is/akin to Bells Palsy. If the later, awesome that you are brave, remain in good spirits and seeing the positive- it goes a long way. If it is supreme muscle control - Wow! The lighting and details are great in this portrait. There are great catch lights in the eyes that shows a cheerful sparkle. You have two asymmetrical subjects in the photo: the first is the ''emotions'' on the face and the second is the thumbs up & thumbs down. This has very clearly met the challenge and is well done - should be in the top ten.', '2014-06-09 18:40:04.000000', NULL, 1),
