(7228037, 1115416, 16106, '<td valign="top">This is a tough one to vote on.<br/>It is a lovely image with a delicate set of pastel colors framed perfectly.<br/>The subject is one of the most perfect examples of symmetry in nature. Google "nautilus symmetry" and you get 146,000 results and if you hit image, you get many images similar to this. <br/>So while I like the image, the subject is so antithetical to the challenge that I''m not sure how to score it. I will think on it and return.</td>', 'This is a tough one to vote on.It is a lovely image with a delicate set of pastel colors framed perfectly.The subject is one of the most perfect examples of symmetry in nature. Google "nautilus symmetry" and you get 146,000 results and if you hit image, you get many images similar to this. So while I like the image, the subject is so antithetical to the challenge that I''m not sure how to score it. I will think on it and return.', '2014-06-12 16:52:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228040, 1116534, 16106, '<td valign="top">a nice use of narrow DOF, and delicate yet vibrant colors make this a top contender. If only you could have gotten that drifting pod over her fingers out into the black, it would have been perfect.</td>', 'a nice use of narrow DOF, and delicate yet vibrant colors make this a top contender. If only you could have gotten that drifting pod over her fingers out into the black, it would have been perfect.', '2014-06-12 16:54:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228041, 1115618, 16106, '<td valign="top">I like the wash of grit here, and while I have been rating the images that get their asymmetry strictly through framing rather poorly, for some reason this one is among my top handful.</td>', 'I like the wash of grit here, and while I have been rating the images that get their asymmetry strictly through framing rather poorly, for some reason this one is among my top handful.', '2014-06-12 16:57:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228044, 1116299, 16106, '<td valign="top">Im not sure if this is more Weston or Cunningham, but it sure is good. The lighting is very strong with two quibbles. I know monitor to monitor will be different but I see no edge at the bottom right, and I miss it, and the pocket of fabric on the left foreground that is lit adds a distracting element. Those are quibbles in a beautiful image. The rim lighting on the left side of the pepper is just perfect.</td>', 'Im not sure if this is more Weston or Cunningham, but it sure is good. The lighting is very strong with two quibbles. I know monitor to monitor will be different but I see no edge at the bottom right, and I miss it, and the pocket of fabric on the left foreground that is lit adds a distracting element. Those are quibbles in a beautiful image. The rim lighting on the left side of the pepper is just perfect.', '2014-06-12 17:01:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228045, 1116464, 16106, '<td valign="top">Clear crisp and clever. I do find the reel''s edge on the upper left fading into the background, but that is the only flaw.</td>', 'Clear crisp and clever. I do find the reel''s edge on the upper left fading into the background, but that is the only flaw.', '2014-06-12 17:03:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228046, 1116433, 16106, '<td valign="top">You claim they are both windows, but one is clearly a door! No points for you!<br/> <br/>Lots of wonderful textures and the quirky framing is deftly handled. Top ten with a shot at a ribbon.</td>', 'You claim they are both windows, but one is clearly a door! No points for you! Lots of wonderful textures and the quirky framing is deftly handled. Top ten with a shot at a ribbon.', '2014-06-12 17:05:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228049, 1115387, 16106, '<td valign="top">How do you make a tomato seem monumental. Topaz and Bear like confidence do help. It is a touch over dark on the upper left where I lose the edge of the tomato into the cutting board, but that is pretty minor in such a lovely image. top ten.</td>', 'How do you make a tomato seem monumental. Topaz and Bear like confidence do help. It is a touch over dark on the upper left where I lose the edge of the tomato into the cutting board, but that is pretty minor in such a lovely image. top ten.', '2014-06-12 17:08:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228050, 1116138, 16106, '<td valign="top">I do wish that poor cow to the right had not had her head cut in half, but this is a great find with nice textures and deftly handled colors. nice use of focus to isolate the subject.</td>', 'I do wish that poor cow to the right had not had her head cut in half, but this is a great find with nice textures and deftly handled colors. nice use of focus to isolate the subject.', '2014-06-12 17:10:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7228053, 1116385, 16106, '<td valign="top">I do not like that I like this one so much. Great textures and concept but in the end you went to a lot of work to make something symmetrical. The two halves you put together look so very much alike. Also I do not care for the trope of spraying water on an object to create texture instead of making the texture that is there work for you. Now that you know what I don''t like, the thing that really pisses me off is that you did all those things I don''t like and made a shot I think deserves the blue. And that I .....well I don''t like it.</td>', 'I do not like that I like this one so much. Great textures and concept but in the end you went to a lot of work to make something symmetrical. The two halves you put together look so very much alike. Also I do not care for the trope of spraying water on an object to create texture instead of making the texture that is there work for you. Now that you know what I don''t like, the thing that really pisses me off is that you did all those things I don''t like and made a shot I think deserves the blue. And that I .....well I don''t like it.', '2014-06-12 17:16:02.000000', NULL, 1),
